{
 "_about": "Customer crawler-v3 routes (DM left out) and the /v1 operations that reach them, from the 2026-10-12 parity audit inventory (auto-sns-agent apps/llm-wiki/content/sessions/2026/10/12/2140-api-portal-crawler-parity/data/inventory.json). When a job adds a /v1 route for a crawler route, it adds the operation here as \"METHOD /v1/path\". byDesign names the board decision that keeps a route out of the portal. An entry ending in \" job\" is the operation in job mode (max_pages above 1), which is how the portal reaches the crawler jobs routes. Each env scores only the entries its own crawler openapi lists (crawler.virev.ai for prod, staging-crawler.virev.ai for staging), so an entry for a crawler route that a rename replaced scores where that route is still served and the successor entry scores where the new route is served; an entry the grammar dropped with no crawler successor (the YouTube batch POSTs, now POST /v1/batch, auto-sns-agent 4f494781d9; LinkedIn search/location, 3203dd2d90) scores only while prod lists it and then shows as crawler_route_gone. \"envs\" limits an entry to the envs it names.",
